Why BigInteger for ID?

Integer:     Max ~2.1 billion rows
BigInteger:  Max ~9.2 quintillion rows (9,223,372,036,854,775,807)

# Real-world scenario:
# Scanning 1000 servers * 1 million files each = 1 billion rows
# Integer would overflow!
Why Numeric(18, 2) for Decimals?

Numeric(18, 2):
    │      │
    │      └─ 2 decimal places
    └─ 18 total digits

Examples:
1234567890123456.78  ✅ Valid (16 digits + 2 decimals = 18)
123.45               ✅ Valid
0.99                 ✅ Valid
1234567890123456.789 ❌ Invalid (19 digits total)

# Why not Float?
Float:  123.456 might become 123.45600000001 (imprecise!)
Numeric: 123.456 is EXACTLY 123.456 (financial accuracy)
