3.1 Schema Design Philosophy
Normalized Design - No Data Duplication:

-- GOOD (Normalized):
tpsm_projects:          tpsm_responses:
+----+-------------+    +----+------------+-------------+
| id | name        |    | id | project_id | question_id |
+----+-------------+    +----+------------+-------------+
| 1  | Project A   |    | 1  | 1          | Q1          |
| 2  | Project B   |    | 2  | 1          | Q2          |
+----+-------------+    | 3  | 2          | Q1          |
                        +----+------------+-------------+

-- BAD (Denormalized):
tpsm_responses_bad:
+----+-------------+-------------+
| id | project_name| question_id |
+----+-------------+-------------+
| 1  | Project A   | Q1          |  ← Name repeated
| 2  | Project A   | Q2          |  ← Name repeated
| 3  | Project B   | Q1          |
+----+-------------+-------------+

Problem: If "Project A" renamed to "Project X":
- Normalized: Update 1 row in projects table
