def _analyze_access_patterns(self, project_id: int) -> Dict:
    patterns = {
        'Hot': (0, 30),      # Accessed in last 30 days
        'Warm': (30, 90),    # 30-90 days
        'Cold': (90, 365),   # 90-365 days
        'Frozen': (365, 36500)  # > 1 year
    }
    
    for pattern_name, (min_days, max_days) in patterns.items():
        min_date = now - timedelta(days=max_days)
        max_date = now - timedelta(days=min_days)
        
        result = db.query(
            func.count(FileMetadata.id),
            func.sum(FileMetadata.size_gb)
        ).filter(
            FileMetadata.accessed_date >= min_date,
            FileMetadata.accessed_date < max_date
        ).first()
Access vs Modification - Key Difference:

Modification Date:
    - When file content changed
    - Indicates data freshness
    - Used for compliance (data retention)

Access Date:
    - When file was read/opened
    - Indicates usage frequency
    - Used for performance optimization

Example:
    File: "sales_report_2020.pdf"
    Created: Jan 2020
    Modified: Jan 2020 (never changed)
    Accessed: Dec 2025 (read monthly)
    
    Age-based tier: Archive (> 5 years old)
    Access-based tier: Hot (accessed recently)
    
    Best tier: Cool (compromise)
    Reasoning: Important to access, but not frequently modified
